### TC-FUNC-AC10-01 | Pricing API — Out of Scope Enforcement

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-FUNC-AC10-01 |
| **AC Reference** | AC10 — Pricing API (actual out-of-pocket cost) is out of scope. Only copay tier label displayed |
| **Scenario** | Verify that no actual dollar cost is displayed — only the copay tier label (Tier 1–4) |
| **Pre-conditions** | Member is logged in. Drug search returns a covered result with a tier value |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Log in as a valid member. 2. Navigate to Pharmacy Benefit Checker. 3. Search for a covered drug. 4. Review the cost section of the results. 5. Verify only the copay tier label is displayed (e.g., "Tier 2"). 6. Verify no dollar amount, deductible calculation, or out-of-pocket cost figure is shown |
| **Expected Result** | Results show only the tier label. No dollar value or pricing API output is present |
| **Pass Criteria** | No dollar amount displayed. Tier label present. No null/blank/error field where pricing data would appear |
| **Severity** | 🟡 Medium |

> ⚠️ **Flag:** AC10 is a negative scope boundary — it defines what should NOT appear rather than what should. Risk: if a blank or "$0" placeholder appears where pricing data would go, it may confuse members. Recommend adding explicit AC for what the UI shows in the cost section when pricing API is not integrated.

